# Stages 4+5: minimize + z-density NPT equilibration + fragment placement
# + restrained re-equilibration + NVT + production of the merged
# substrate/liquid slab, in ONE continuous LAMMPS session -- confirmed
# live 2026-11-06 that splitting these into separate `lmp` invocations
# (minimize, write a checkpoint, NVT re-reads it) is NOT robust for this
# system's `bond_style hybrid harmonic`: write_data silently drops its
# Bond/Angle/Dihedral Coeffs sections regardless of type count, and
# read_restart across invocations lost bond coeffs too (inconsistently,
# worse after deduplicating down to a handful of types, not better -- see
# scripts/dedup_lammps_bonded_types.py's docstring for the deduplication
# itself, which is still worth doing on its own merits, just not
# sufficient for this). Keeping every stage in one session sidesteps the
# whole class of problem: there is no serialize/deserialize boundary to
# get wrong. This is also why the fragment's post-equilibration
# repositioning below is done with LAMMPS's own `xcm()`/`displace_atoms`
# inside this same run, instead of a second Python pass between two `lmp`
# invocations -- there is no file in between to lose bond coeffs from.
#
# All dynamics stages freeze the substrate (it was already relaxed on its
# own terms by step2_substrate.smk and should not be re-relaxed or
# thermally perturbed here -- this pipeline treats it as a static wall,
# matching sf1d's own SCF model): `fix setforce 0 0 0` for minimize
# (which moves every atom regardless of any time-integration group),
# simply no integrator fix at all for the thermostatted/barostatted runs
# (which only move atoms covered by one), and every barostat below uses
# `dilate mobile` so a box-length rescale only rescales the `mobile` group
# it's attached to, never the substrate's absolute coordinates.
#
# Confirmed live 2026-11-08, from the real flow2-ai production run's own
# checkpoints (merged.data -> minimized.data -> nvt.data ->
# production.data): the liquid column's z-extent and the fragment's
# position both changed drastically within the FIRST 20 ps of the old
# fixed-volume NVT stage (PotEng dropped ~13,000 kcal/mol in the first
# 2-5 ps for both species) -- the box's z-length, set by merge_slab.py
# from a single raw, unequilibrated GROMACS->LAMMPS snapshot's occupied
# thickness, was not at this merged system's true NVT/NPT-equilibrium
# density. Under fixed volume, the liquid could only "fix" that mismatch
# by redistributing internally: for ST that meant an outright ~10 A
# vacuum gap at the box's periodic z-seam; for MMA, a long near-zero
# depletion stretch next to one (real) substrate face and a denser,
# structurally different pileup at the other -- an asymmetry that should
# not exist between two faces of the same substrate material. The single
# fragment molecule, wherever step2_dilute.smk's GROMACS packing had
# happened to leave it, got swept along with that same fast transient
# into the lowest-density region in both species -- not a deliberate
# placement, a side effect of starting from the wrong volume. Stages
# 4b-4d below replace the old single fixed-volume NVT with: a real
# z-direction barostat equilibration (only z, keep x,y fixed -- they
# must stay commensurate with the substrate's lattice, the same
# constraint GROMACS's own npt_semiiso.mdp already respects in
# step2_dilute.smk), then a deliberate fragment placement at the
# resulting bulk-arc midpoint (computed from this run's OWN zhi/zlo and
# xcm(), not guessed), then a short restrained re-equilibration so the
# solvent can relax around the newly-placed fragment without it drifting
# straight back to the seam before production even starts.
#
# The barostat is `fix press/berendsen`, NOT `fix npt`/Nose-Hoover --
# confirmed live 2026-11-08 by direct comparison on this exact system
# (ST's merged.data): `fix npt mobile npt ... z 1.0 1.0 1000.0 dilate
# mobile` never converges here at all, not even to a self-consistent
# non-literal target -- temperature ran away to a stable-but-wrong ~465 K
# plateau and pressure to ~137,000 atm regardless of whether the target
# was a literal 1 atm or the system's own pre-barostat pressure reading
# (~19,375 atm); the frozen substrate's own enormous internal ionic
# virial (E_coul ~ -1.4e6 kcal/mol) swamps the only lever the barostat
# has (the liquid's own volume), and Nose-Hoover's extended-Lagrangian
# inertia turns that irreducible mismatch into a runaway heating
# feedback loop. `fix press/berendsen` (no inertia, a direct per-step
# volume rescale toward the target) does NOT have this failure mode:
# with the SAME literal 1 atm target it reached a genuinely stable 300 K
# / ~133,700 atm steady state and -- more importantly -- its z-length
# contracted from 109.33 to 100.87 A within 0.5 ps and then held flat for
# the rest of a 10 ps test run, an 8.46 A contraction matching almost
# exactly the 8.45 A the real 10 ns flow2-ai production run slowly
# drifted toward under passive fixed-volume NVT (see the earlier
# paragraph). Found by example in the sibling
# ../2026-10-28-generate-aa-pama repo's
# in/335_polymer_in_solvent_on_substrate_npt/npt.lmp.template, which
# barostats a similarly substrate-adjacent liquid this same way (its own
# `dilate partial` -- a literal value, not a group-ID, specific to
# `press/berendsen`'s keyword syntax and different from `fix npt`'s
# `dilate <group-ID>`, confirmed live 2026-11-08 the two are not
# interchangeable) with `barostat_damping: 25000` (fs) and `modulus:
# 10000` (atm, a plausible bulk modulus for a simple alkane liquid) --
# reused here unchanged rather than re-tuned from scratch.
units real
atom_style full
boundary p p p

bond_style hybrid harmonic
angle_style hybrid harmonic
dihedral_style hybrid multi/harmonic
special_bonds lj 0.0 0.0 0.5 coul 0.0 0.0 0.5

read_data merged.data

pair_style lj/cut/coul/long {{ params.cutoff }}
kspace_style pppm {{ params.kspace_accuracy }}
include merged_pair_coeffs.lmp
pair_modify mix geometric

group mobile type 1:{{ params.n_org_types }}
group substrate type {{ params.n_org_types + 1 }}:{{ params.n_org_types + 2 }}
velocity substrate set 0.0 0.0 0.0

# Stage 5's density profiles need the single adsorbing fragment split out
# from the many hexadecane molecules within `mobile`. Confirmed live
# 2026-11-06 for both ST and MMA (unwrapped.gro / converted.lmp): a
# fragment_length=1 "CH3-{species}-CH3" capped repeat unit is written by
# GROMACS/polyply as THREE separate molecule-IDs (cap, core, cap --
# residues "1CH3"/"2{species}"/"3CH3" in the .gro), always 1-3 since the
# fragment is always the very first molecule in topol.top's [molecules]
# section (see rules/step2_dilute.smk). Hexadecane molecule-IDs start
# right after at 4 and run up to merge_slab.py's max_org_molid (passed in
# below; the substrate itself gets the one molid right after that, not
# needed here since it's already selected by atom type above).
group fragment molecule 1:3
group hexadecane molecule 4:{{ params.max_org_molid }}

neighbor 2.0 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 0 check yes

thermo 50
thermo_style custom step pe ebond eangle edihed evdwl ecoul elong

# --- Stage 4a: minimize (see module docstring on why E_vdwl stays large
# and positive throughout -- that is the substrate's own normal
# ionic-LJ baseline, not an unresolved clash) ---
min_style cg
fix freeze_substrate substrate setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
minimize {{ params.etol }} {{ params.ftol }} {{ params.maxiter }} {{ params.maxeval }}
unfix freeze_substrate

write_data minimized.data
write_restart minimized.restart

velocity mobile create {{ params.temperature_K }} {{ params.seed }} mom yes rot yes dist gaussian

timestep {{ params.timestep_fs }}
thermo 500

# `fix nvt`/`fix npt` on a given group already thermostat/barostat
# correctly (each builds its own temp/press computes scoped to that
# group's real DOF). But the plain `temp`/`press` thermo keywords resolve
# to the default "all"-group computes, which divide by (3*N_all - 3) even
# though the frozen substrate contributes zero kinetic energy -- confirmed
# live 2026-11-06 for `temp` (read ~192 K at a 300 K target; the dynamics
# were never wrong, only that display). Scoped computes below avoid the
# same display artifact for the new stages' `press` column.
compute mobtemp mobile temp
# `compute pressure` requires group "all" (the virial is inherently a
# global per-box quantity, confirmed live 2026-11-08 -- "Compute pressure
# must use group all") -- only the temperature-compute argument used for
# its kinetic term is group-scoped.
compute mobpress all pressure mobtemp

# --- Stage 4b: z-density Berendsen barostat equilibration, substrate +
# lateral box fixed. `dilate partial` (a literal value for THIS fix
# style, see module docstring) means ONLY atoms in `mobile` get their
# coordinates rescaled as the box's z-length adjusts -- the substrate's
# absolute position never moves. x,y are not barostatted at all (no x/y
# keyword below), keeping the box commensurate with the substrate's
# lattice throughout, the same constraint GROMACS's own npt_semiiso.mdp
# respects in step2_dilute.smk. A separate `fix nvt` still controls
# temperature -- `press/berendsen` only rescales volume, it has no
# thermostat of its own (unlike `fix npt`).
thermo_style custom step c_mobtemp c_mobpress pe evdwl ecoul elong

fix npt_z_temp mobile nvt temp {{ params.temperature_K }} {{ params.temperature_K }} 100.0
fix npt_z mobile press/berendsen z {{ params.pressure_atm }} {{ params.pressure_atm }} &
    {{ params.pressure_damp_fs }} modulus {{ params.modulus_atm }} dilate partial

run {{ params.npt_z_nsteps }}

unfix npt_z
unfix npt_z_temp

write_data npt_equilibrated.data
write_restart npt_equilibrated.restart

# --- Stage 4c: move the fragment to the middle of the now-equilibrated
# liquid arc. The substrate's own [sub_zmin, sub_zmax] never changes
# (dilate mobile above), so it's passed in as a fixed param; the box's
# current zhi/zlo (it may have shrunk or grown from merged.data's
# original values during stage 4b) and the fragment's current
# center-of-mass z are read live from this running session via LAMMPS's
# own box-bound keywords and xcm() -- no second Python pass, no
# write_data/read_data round trip, see module docstring on why that
# matters for this system's bond_style hybrid harmonic. The liquid
# occupies one contiguous arc from sub_zmax, up through the box's
# periodic wrap, down to sub_zmin (confirmed live 2026-11-08 the
# substrate is a single contiguous block, not split across the periodic
# boundary); its midpoint is sub_zmax + arc_length/2.
variable sub_zmin equal {{ params.sub_zmin }}
variable sub_zmax equal {{ params.sub_zmax }}
variable arc_length equal "zhi - zlo - (v_sub_zmax - v_sub_zmin)"
variable target_z equal "v_sub_zmax + v_arc_length / 2.0"
variable frag_cz equal "xcm(fragment,z)"
variable dz equal "v_target_z - v_frag_cz"

print "fragment centroid z = ${frag_cz}, target bulk-arc midpoint z = ${target_z}, displacing by ${dz}"
displace_atoms fragment move 0.0 0.0 ${dz} units box

# Moving the fragment this way drops it straight into whatever hexadecane
# already occupied that spot -- resolve the resulting steric overlap with
# the same minimizer as stage 4a before resuming dynamics.
fix freeze_substrate substrate setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
minimize {{ params.etol }} {{ params.ftol }} {{ params.maxiter }} {{ params.maxeval }}
unfix freeze_substrate

# --- Stage 4d: short restrained re-equilibration. The fragment is held
# near its new target position with a per-atom spring back to that
# position (`spring/self`, the LAMMPS equivalent of GROMACS position
# restraints) while the solvent relaxes around it; the z-barostat stays
# on, now scoped to `hexadecane` only (not `mobile`) so it never fights
# the fragment's restraint -- `dilate partial` on this fix only rescales
# hexadecane atoms (its own fix-group), leaving the restrained fragment's
# coordinates alone when the box adjusts. Separate `fix nvt` per group
# for temperature control, same reason as stage 4b: `press/berendsen`
# only rescales volume.
compute hextemp hexadecane temp
compute hexpress all pressure hextemp
compute fragtemp fragment temp
thermo_style custom step c_hextemp c_hexpress c_fragtemp pe evdwl ecoul elong

fix frag_nvt fragment nvt temp {{ params.temperature_K }} {{ params.temperature_K }} 100.0
fix restrain_frag fragment spring/self {{ params.restraint_k }}
fix hex_nvt hexadecane nvt temp {{ params.temperature_K }} {{ params.temperature_K }} 100.0
fix npt_hex hexadecane press/berendsen z {{ params.pressure_atm }} {{ params.pressure_atm }} &
    {{ params.pressure_damp_fs }} modulus {{ params.modulus_atm }} dilate partial

run {{ params.restrained_npt_nsteps }}

unfix npt_hex
unfix hex_nvt
unfix restrain_frag
unfix frag_nvt

write_data restrained.data
write_restart restrained.restart

# --- Stage 4e: final NVT equilibration, restraint released, box length
# fixed at whatever stage 4b/4d settled on (no barostat from here on) ---
thermo_style custom step c_mobtemp pe ebond eangle edihed evdwl ecoul elong

fix 1 mobile nvt temp {{ params.temperature_K }} {{ params.temperature_K }} 100.0

run {{ params.nsteps }}

write_data nvt.data
write_restart nvt.restart

# --- Stage 5: production NVT, with z-resolved number-density profiles
# for the fragment and for hexadecane (chis_x reads the contact-vs-bulk
# ratio off these, forcefield/chi_chis_from_md.md step 2). One shared
# compute chunk/atom bins the whole box along z (origin 0.0 handles the
# box's slightly-negative xlo/ylo/zlo from merge_slab.py fine -- LAMMPS
# bins via floor((x-origin)/delta), which is well-defined for negative x
# too); two separate `fix ave/chunk` average each group's atom count into
# those bins. Deliberately NOT "ave running": keeping each window's
# average independent (the default) lets stage 6 check whether the
# profile is still drifting late in the run (a single fragment molecule's
# sampling of contact-vs-bulk could in principle not have converged in
# any finite run -- see config.yaml's slab.production_ns comment) instead
# of silently trusting one cumulative number.
compute cz all chunk/atom bin/1d z 0.0 {{ params.bin_width_angstrom }} units box

fix dfrag fragment ave/chunk {{ params.chunk_nevery }} {{ params.chunk_nrepeat }} {{ params.chunk_nfreq }} cz density/number file fragment_density.profile
fix dhex hexadecane ave/chunk {{ params.chunk_nevery }} {{ params.chunk_nrepeat }} {{ params.chunk_nfreq }} cz density/number file hexadecane_density.profile

thermo {{ params.chunk_nfreq }}
run {{ params.production_nsteps }}

write_data production.data
write_restart production.restart
